 ## Overview
-NeRF Volumetric Rendering synthesizes novel views by querying a neural radiance field (a coordinate MLP) along camera rays and accumulating outputs using differentiable volume rendering [S1][S2, S3, unofficial]. It solves the view synthesis problem by optimizing a continuous 5D function (spatial location and viewing direction) to predict volume density and view-dependent color [S1]. Unlike single-stage uniform sampling, this method employs a two-stage hierarchical sampling strategy: a coarse network estimates density to guide finer sampling in high-density regions, reducing aliasing and improving geometric detail [S5, unofficial]. It operates on a flat batch of rays rather than a spatial grid, enabling efficient training on randomly sampled rays [S3, unofficial].
+NeRF Volumetric Rendering synthesizes novel views by querying a neural radiance field (a coordinate MLP) along camera rays and accumulating outputs using differentiable volume rendering [S1][S3, unofficial]. It solves the view synthesis problem by optimizing a continuous 5D function (spatial location and viewing direction) to predict volume density and view-dependent color [S1]. Unlike single-stage uniform sampling, this method employs a two-stage hierarchical sampling strategy: a coarse network estimates density to guide finer sampling in high-density regions, reducing aliasing and improving geometric detail [S7, unofficial]. It operates on a flat batch of rays rather than a spatial grid, enabling efficient training on randomly sampled rays [S3, unofficial].
 
